{"abstract":"Little effort has been devoted to studying the emotional experience of designers over time. Using sentiment analysis, we explore a unique corpus of designers’ written reflections on 15 different design processes. We investigate how positive and negative sentiment in the reflections change over the course of a three-month design project. Our findings indicate that change in sentiment is not attributable to time alone, but rather to different phases and methods employed by the design teams. Finally, we discuss implications and future avenues for both our results and for using sentiment analysis in HCI research.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Frich Pedersen, Jonas","Inie, Nanna","Halskov, Kim","Dalsgaard, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-247732"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","title":"ACM Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Design experience","Design process","Sentiment analysis"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a sentiment analysis of design reflections from design projects","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85052022063","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-247732","identifier":[{"id":"85052022063","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-cf368464-c8bd-4692-bb2e-e6ef9c15ce44"],"keyword":["Design experience","Design process","Sentiment analysis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-57EDAB272947274DC03500E59AF3FA55"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Information Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jonas","key":"frichpedersenpau","last":"Frich Pedersen","locid":"1f394a37-c0c2-40b9-b2b5-45e5021746c1","name":"Frich Pedersen, Jonas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"3d920ab1-3bf7-4959-b38f-7460123101c4","name":"Inie, Nanna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Kim","key":"halskovpau","last":"Halskov","locid":"3043cd86-47ac-46ef-b907-a367b2f0ca5a","name":"Halskov, Kim","orcid":"0000-0001-7448-7577","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"07bc29a5-f5da-47d0-8290-fd9ab3659541","name":"Dalsgaard, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-9884-7178","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3170427.3188444","eisbn":["9781450356206","9781450356213"],"isbn":["9781450356213"],"publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Engage with CHI","title":"CHI 2018 - Extended Abstracts of the 2018 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85052022063"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-cf368464-c8bd-4692-bb2e-e6ef9c15ce44"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A Sentiment Analysis of Design Reflections from Design Projects","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-247732","year":"2018","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"Design ideas are commonly used as an indicator of success of design methods and processes. Yet it is very rarely defined what precisely constitutes \"an idea\", and how such an idea manifests itself to the researcher. This paper presents an examination of design idea definitions based on a thorough study of 75 research contributions. We construct a typology of seven definitions of design ideas. The purpose of the typology is to offer shared definitions and descriptions of design ideas to design and creativity researchers, aiding a higher degree of specificity when studying and analyzing the emergence of ideas in design processes.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Inie, Nanna","Dalsgaard, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-183641"],"event":{"acronym":"CANDC","title":"ACM Creativity & Cognition"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Creativity","Design ideas","Design processes","Design theory","Idea generation","Ideation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a typology of design ideas","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85025700074","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-183641","identifier":[{"id":"85025700074","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-5f309c86-75d5-4e04-81a6-84c304c5113a"],"keyword":["Creativity","Design ideas","Design processes","Design theory","Idea definition","Idea generation","Ideation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-62660108927401CC775E3E3628F0BFDC"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Centre for Advanced Visualisation and Interaction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"3d920ab1-3bf7-4959-b38f-7460123101c4","name":"Inie, Nanna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"07bc29a5-f5da-47d0-8290-fd9ab3659541","name":"Dalsgaard, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-9884-7178","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"eisbn":["9781450344036"],"pages":"393-406","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2017 ACM SIGCHI Conference on Creativity and Cognition","title":"C and C 2017 - Proceedings of the 2017 ACM SIGCHI Conference on Creativity and Cognition"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85025700074"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-5f309c86-75d5-4e04-81a6-84c304c5113a"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"A Typology of Design Ideas","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-183641","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we present an in-depth survey of how interaction designers use tools to capture, manage and collaborate on ideas. We observe that designers report very unique processes with various tools, and that no dominant tool is present for idea capture and development. Our discoveries are summarized into three key insights, suggesting ways for interaction design research to support these practices.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Inie, Nanna","Dalsgaard, Peter"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-213500"],"event":{"acronym":"CHI","end":"2017-05-11","place":"Denver, us","start":"2017-05-06","title":"Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems","year":"2017"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Idea Development","Idea management","Ideas","Tools"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how interaction designers use tools to capture manage and collaborate on ideas","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85019608684","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-213500","identifier":[{"id":"85019608684","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-93bb2f80-95ab-4443-9c30-bf39a3be12c8"],"keyword":["Idea development","Idea management","Ideas","Tools"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-9F777C39B514337A11102E99D62ABD40"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Centre for Advanced Visualisation and Interaction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"3d920ab1-3bf7-4959-b38f-7460123101c4","name":"Inie, Nanna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"07bc29a5-f5da-47d0-8290-fd9ab3659541","name":"Dalsgaard, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-9884-7178","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Gloria","key":"markpedh","last":"Mark","name":"Mark, Gloria","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Susan","key":"fussellpedh","last":"Fussell","name":"Fussell, Susan","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3027063.3053210","eisbn":["9781450346566"],"isbn":["ISBN: 9781450346566"],"pages":"2668-2675","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Explore, Innovate, Inspire","title":"CHI 2017 Extended Abstracts - Proceedings of the 2017 ACM SIGCHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85019608684"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-93bb2f80-95ab-4443-9c30-bf39a3be12c8"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"How Interaction Designers use Tools to Capture, Manage, and Collaborate on Ideas","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-213500","year":"2017","yearsub":"2017"}
{"abstract":"The aim of the workshop is to examine and discuss how computers can support, enrich, and transform collaborative creative processes. By exploring and combining methodological, theoretical, and design- oriented perspectives, we wish to examine the implications, potentials, and limitations of different approaches to providing digital support for collaborative creativity. Participation in the workshop requires participants to actively document and identify salient themes in one or more examples of computer- supported collaborative creativity, and the resulting material will serve as the empirical grounding for workshop discussions.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Dalsgaard, Peter","Inie, Nanna","Hansen, Nicolai Brodersen"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-150332"],"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how can computers support enrich and transform collaborative creativity","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85025671855","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-150332","identifier":[{"id":"85025671855","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-24957f06-4696-4f03-a7b2-8e5ef03100eb"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-EB25D637BA4029A5530B62D4A7C5797B"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Centre for Advanced Visualisation and Interaction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Peter","key":"dalsgaardpau","last":"Dalsgaard","locid":"07bc29a5-f5da-47d0-8290-fd9ab3659541","name":"Dalsgaard, Peter","orcid":"0000-0001-9884-7178","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"3d920ab1-3bf7-4959-b38f-7460123101c4","name":"Inie, Nanna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolai Brodersen","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","locid":"62bc8308-331d-431a-9fa3-c68827582a32","name":"Hansen, Nicolai Brodersen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3059454.3059483","eisbn":["9781450344036"],"pages":"554-560","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2017 ACM SIGCHI Conference on Creativity and Cognition","title":"C&amp;C '17"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85025671855"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-24957f06-4696-4f03-a7b2-8e5ef03100eb"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"How can computers support, enrich, and transform collaborative creativity","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-150332","year":"2017","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"This position paper outlines four types of design idea indicators that provide four starting points for exploration of the emergence of design ideas from a micro perspective. The results are derived from two empirical studies of design processes. The research builds on the assumption that we need better understanding and definition of design idea emergence and transformation in order to systematically explore the creative process.","author_count":1,"contributors":["Inie, Nanna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-157425"],"event":{"end":"2015-06-25","place":"Glasgow, gb","start":"2015-06-25","title":"Supporting Creative Design Processes in Blended Interaction Spaces","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"1 contributor","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Creativity","Design processes","Emergence","Ideas","Ideation"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"identifying the emergence of design ideas","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-157425","ids":["au-31220956-2470-497b-8bd8-acc98d3a2000"],"keyword":["Creativity","Ideas","design processes","emergence","ideation"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-07FBBBFD809A5D84B1CF772068334067"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Centre for Advanced Visualisation and Interaction"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"3d920ab1-3bf7-4959-b38f-7460123101c4","name":"Inie, Nanna","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-31220956-2470-497b-8bd8-acc98d3a2000"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Identifying the emergence of design ideas","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-157425","year":"2015","yearsub":"2015"}
